  "details": "# Issue\n\nAudio playback, such as speech and menu sounds, may at times be \"cut off\" at the start and end of playback, **by upwards of one second,** resulting in strange or difficult to follow audio.\n\n# Example\n\nYou are in another instance with a user who uses voice activation to speak, and frequently pauses in-between words. When they pause and resume speech, the start and end of their words may be cut off by upwards of one second. As they pause frequently between words, this means many words may sound garbled or be lost as their mic activates and deactivates.\n\n# Note\n\nThis **does not effect outgoing audio.** Users on LIVE branches notice no change in audio quality nor the issues outline above **from** users on the BETA branch. The issue only affects **incoming** audio.",
